 "about": "The halo model with red and blue galaxies fitted jointly to the nine core FLAMINGO snapshots (fits/hmc_rb_fit.py, k_max = 0.52 h/Mpc). a1_snap: the linear-alignment amplitude A1 of the per-snapshot HMc fit with a free share of nonlinear power and no satellites (fits/hmc_alpha_fit.py, alpha_cap_nosat), with its error; a1_joint[model]: the effective amplitude of each joint model at each snapshot; chi2_nu[model]: its chi2/nu. Models: 1p one population, A1 ((1+z)/1.62)^eta1; 1pB one population, A1 b_g(z)/1.5; rbS every galaxy aligned like its host halo, A_h [f_red b_red + kappa_b f_blue b_blue]/1.5, kappa_b free (1pB at kappa_b = 1), fiducial red fractions; rbS_zm the same with the Zu and Mandelbaum fractions at every z; rbH centrals only, A_h [f_rc b_rc + kappa_b f_bc b_bc], blue torquing; rbF21 red and blue centrals with constant amplitudes (Fortuna et al. 2021 Eqs. 3-4). f_rc, f_bc, f_rs, f_bs: red and blue central and satellite fractions of the sample (Zu and Mandelbaum 2016 at z <= 0.1, Tinker et al. 2013 at 0.36 to 0.88, held above; analysis/roman_dchi2/v6/halo_redblue.py); b_g: the HOD galaxy bias.",
